{"tool_name":"metaarray","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"metaarray","home":"http://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/metaArray.html","license":"GPL-2.0","summary":"Data transformation for meta-analysis of microarray data: Transformation of gene expression data to signed probability scale (MCMC/EM methods). Combined differential expression on raw scale: Weighted Z-score after stabilizing mean-variance relation within platform.","addition_date":"2017-01-17T15:02:23Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:58:51Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"version":["1.52.0"],"collections":["BioConductor"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:metaarray","credit":[{"email":"hyung_won_choi@nuhs.edu.sg","name":"Hyungwon Choi","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/metaArray.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Formatting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0335"}]}],"name":"metaArray","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"bioconductor_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/1471-2105-8-364","metadata":{"abstract":"Background: With the explosion in data generated using microarray technology by different investigators working on similar experiments, it is of interest to combine results across multiple studies. Results: In this article, we describe a general probabilistic framework for combining high-throughput genomic data from several related microarray experiments using mixture models. A key feature of the model is the use of latent variables that represent quantities that can be combined across diverse platforms. We consider two methods for estimation of an index termed the probability of expression (POE). The first, reported in previous work by the authors, involves Markov Chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) techniques. The second method is a faster algorithm 